From e94df8e3e29f154a5aa5bbacca68f9d61c51566d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:35:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: ship a logical-decoding config for the regression
 suite

Every test in the suite opens a logical replication slot, which a default
server cannot do: `wal_level` has to be `logical` and there have to be
replication slots and WAL senders to spare. The Makefile states the
requirement in a comment above the `installcheck` target and leaves satisfying
it to whoever runs the tests, by editing `postgresql.conf` and starting the
server themselves.

A pg_regress `--temp-instance` starts its own server, so there is no
configuration to edit beforehand; what it does take is a `--temp-config`
fragment. Add the three settings the comment asks for as `logical.conf`, so
the requirement travels with the suite instead of living only in prose, and a
caller can point pg_regress at it.
---
 logical.conf | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 logical.conf

diff --git a/logical.conf b/logical.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..107daf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/logical.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+wal_level = logical
+max_replication_slots = 10
+max_wal_senders = 10
